#
# One exclusion list for every image: all Dockerfiles build with the repository
# root as their context, so this file decides what the daemon receives seven
# times over.
#
# What must stay in the context, because an image copies it:
#   packages/ground-truth/data   -> the simulator image
#   db/migrations                -> the init image
#   packages/contracts           -> the init image (schemas, embedding.json)
#                                   and the mock decision service image
#   infra/mosquitto              -> the broker image (conf, acl, credentials)
#   pnpm-workspace.yaml, package.json, pnpm-lock.yaml, tsconfig.base.json,
#   apps/, pyproject.toml, uv.lock, tools/init  -> the node and init images
# Kept because they are small and the bind mounts of compose.yaml read them
# from the host anyway: data/manual, data/SHA256SUMS, data/fixtures.

# Secrets never enter a build context: they come from the environment only.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Version control and local tool state (a linked worktree under these
# directories is a whole checkout of this repository).
.git
.claude
.worktrees

# Installed dependencies.
**/node_modules
**/.venv

# Build output and caches.
**/dist
**/build
**/coverage
.cache
.rebuild
tools/manual-build/.build
# Bytecode a host test run leaves beside the sources: the init image copies
# tools/init/src whole, and a stray .pyc would only invalidate that layer.
**/__pycache__

# Large or generated data: the dataset arrives by download into a bind mount
# and the models into a volume, never through an image layer (ground rules 5 and 6,
# CONTRIBUTING.md).
data/metropt3
data/byo-manual
data/models

# Reports and logs written by a previous run.
reports
**/playwright-report
**/test-results
**/*.log
